  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>Thomas S. Blake, grocer, is listed in <ref target="civic?id=Pelham%20Street">Pelham Street</ref> from 1867 to 1910. He is at No. 11 from 1869 to 1885, and at No. 226 from 1890, after the street was renumbered. A T. S. Blake with no trade is listed in Pelham Street in 1865 and 1866, probably the same man.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>H. Harper is next door from 1865 to 1872, and C. Thomas Lucas at No. 9 from 1868 to 1876. From 1873 to 1878 Mrs Susan Rancie, grocer, is on the other side, so two grocers stood side by side. Mrs C. Sabiston, draper, is at No. 13 in 1879 and 1880. After the renumbering, W. J. Patterson, grocer, is at No. 222 in 1890, and John Hatton, butcher, from 1895 to 1910.</p>
      </div>
